From ff5554039f9480908b34fa1b9e53b8957ae0b97b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dameng <dameng@local>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:51:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] EDBT v4 B2: shared deterministic strict-fit mapper for
 all migration policies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the v3 per-cycle capacity-accumulation hot-set (whose boundary
segment could push selected logical bytes past the DRAM budget — observed
as 35 overshoot rows in the B1 equivalence trace, max +300,396,210 bytes)
with one shared strict-fit mapper in policy_mapper.hpp:

- comparator (total, deterministic): score descending, then table name,
  chunk id, column id ascending;
- selection: a segment is placed on DRAM only when segment_bytes <=
  remaining_budget; oversized segments are skipped and later, smaller
  segments may still fit;
- identical rule for every migration policy (our_full, our_freq
  [--ablate_d1, our_no_plan], and cost_c3_greedy from B3) — only the
  priority provider differs, never the selection rule.

Daemon promote order = comparator order over selected segments; demote
order = reverse comparator order over unselected; replica keep set and GC
follow the same selected set. Decision trace rows now carry the mapper's
own remaining-budget state (remaining_budget_before/after), and
selected=true implies fits_remaining=true.

Smoke (20s, JOB all-113, c05 3.47/100/0.95, trace on): 16 cycles, zero
selected-and-not-fitting rows, max selected bytes per cycle 3,725,888,077
<= 3,725,884,160 budget, zero comparator-order violations.
